/-!
# Ring class field checks on nonmaximal quadratic and maximal cubic orders

This file checks the ring class field `ringClassField O` and its Artin reciprocity isomorphism
`ringClassArtinEquiv O : Pic O ≃* Gal(ringClassField O / K)` against concrete orders in degree two
and degree three, consuming `GlobalNumberFields.intAddMulOrder` and
`GlobalNumberFields.maximalNumberFieldOrder` directly without reconstructing orders or ideals
locally:

1. **Orders of trivial ring class field in imaginary quadratic fields.** Combining
   `ringClassArtinEquiv` (`subsingleton_gal_ringClassField_iff`, `ringClassField_eq_bot_iff`) with
   the local-factor classification of imaginary quadratic orders of class number one
   (`NumberFieldOrder.card_pic_intAddMulOrder_eq_one_iff`), `ringClassField (intAddMulOrder K f)`
   is trivial over an imaginary quadratic field `K` iff `𝓞 K` is a principal ideal domain and
   `(discr K, f)` is `(D, 1)`, `(D, 2)` with `D ≡ 1 (mod 8)`, `(-3, 2)`, `(-3, 3)`, or `(-4, 2)`.

2. **The nonmaximal order `ℤ + 2ℤ[i]` (`intAddMulOrder K 2`) in `K = ℚ(i)`.** Here `discr O = -16`
   and conductor `𝔣 = 2 𝓞 K`. Although `#(𝓞 K ⧸ 2 𝓞 K)ˣ = 2` and `#(O ⧸ 2 𝓞 K)ˣ = φ(2) = 1`, the
   unit-index correction `[(𝓞 K)ˣ : Oˣ] = 2` (`±i ∉ ℤ + 2ℤ[i]`) cancels the residue-unit factor
   `2 / (1 · 2) = 1`, so `Pic (intAddMulOrder K 2)` is trivial. Through `ringClassArtinEquiv`,
   `Gal(ringClassField (intAddMulOrder K 2) / K)` is trivial and
   `ringClassField (intAddMulOrder K 2) = ⊥` (`= K`). Consequently every invertible proper
   fractional ideal of `ℤ + 2ℤ[i]` is principal, and every maximal ideal of `ℤ[i]` prime to `2` is
   generated by an element of `ℤ + 2ℤ[i]`. By contrast, for every conductor `f > 2`,
   `ringClassField (intAddMulOrder K f) ≠ ⊥`.

3. **The maximal order of the totally real cubic field `ℚ(ζ₇ + ζ₇⁻¹)` (`maximalRealSubfield L` in
   `ℚ(ζ₇)`).** Because `ringClassField` and `ringClassArtinEquiv` carry no quadratic hypothesis on
   the base field, they apply directly to `maximalNumberFieldOrder (maximalRealSubfield L)`, of
   degree `3` and discriminant `49`. Since `𝓞 (maximalRealSubfield L)` is a principal ideal domain,
   `Pic` of its maximal order is trivial, so `Gal(ringClassField O / L⁺)` is trivial and
   `ringClassField O = hilbertClassField L⁺ = ⊥`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.ClassFieldTheory.subsingleton_gal_ringClassField_intAddMulOrder_iff` and
  `TauCeti.ClassFieldTheory.ringClassField_intAddMulOrder_eq_bot_iff`: classification of imaginary
  quadratic orders `ℤ + f 𝓞 K` whose ring class field equals `K`.
* `TauCeti.ClassFieldTheory.discr_intAddMulOrder_two_four`,
  `TauCeti.ClassFieldTheory.index_range_unitsMap_intAddMulOrder_two_four`,
  `TauCeti.ClassFieldTheory.card_units_quotient_span_two_four`,
  `TauCeti.ClassFieldTheory.natCard_pic_intAddMulOrder_two_four`: invariants and unit-index
  cancellation `2 / (1 · 2) = 1` for `ℤ + 2ℤ[i]` in `ℚ(i)`.
* `TauCeti.ClassFieldTheory.subsingleton_gal_ringClassField_intAddMulOrder_two_four`,
  `TauCeti.ClassFieldTheory.ringClassField_intAddMulOrder_two_four`,
  `TauCeti.ClassFieldTheory.ringClassField_intAddMulOrder_ne_bot_of_two_lt_of_four`:
  `Gal(H_O / ℚ(i))` is trivial and `H_O = ⊥` at `f = 2`, whereas `H_O ≠ ⊥` for every `f > 2`.
* `TauCeti.ClassFieldTheory.isPrincipal_of_invertibleProperFractionalIdeals_intAddMulOrder_two_four`
  and `TauCeti.ClassFieldTheory.exists_mem_intAddMulOrder_two_span_eq_of_four`: principality and
  splitting consequences for `ℤ + 2ℤ[i]`.
* `TauCeti.ClassFieldTheory.discr_maximalNumberFieldOrder_maximalRealSubfield_seven`,
  `TauCeti.ClassFieldTheory.subsingleton_gal_ringClassField_maximalRealSubfield_seven`,
  `TauCeti.ClassFieldTheory.ringClassField_maximalNumberFieldOrder_maximalRealSubfield_seven`,
  `TauCeti.ClassFieldTheory.hilbertClassField_maximalRealSubfield_seven`: `Gal(H_O / L⁺)` is
  trivial and `H_O = hilbertClassField L⁺ = ⊥` for the maximal order of `L⁺ = ℚ(ζ₇ + ζ₇⁻¹)`.

## References

* D. A. Cox, *Primes of the Form x² + ny²*, §7 (Theorem 7.24) and §9 (Theorem 9.18).
* G. S. Kopp and J. C. Lagarias, *Class Field Theory for Orders of Number Fields*, Theorem 1.1.
* L. C. Washington, *Introduction to Cyclotomic Fields*, Proposition 2.16.
-/

public noncomputable section

open NumberField TauCeti.GlobalNumberFields TauCeti.GlobalNumberFields.NumberFieldOrder
  TauCeti.NumberField

namespace TauCeti.ClassFieldTheory

/-! ### Imaginary quadratic orders with trivial ring class field -/

section ImaginaryQuadratic

variable {K : Type} [Field K] [NumberField K] [IsTotallyComplex K]

/-- In an imaginary quadratic field `K`, the Picard group of `ℤ + f 𝓞 K` is trivial iff `𝓞 K` is a
principal ideal domain and `(discr K, f)` is one of `(D, 1)`, `(D, 2)` with `D ≡ 1 (mod 8)`,
`(-3, 2)`, `(-3, 3)`, or `(-4, 2)`. -/
theorem subsingleton_pic_intAddMulOrder_iff (hK : Module.finrank ℚ K = 2) (f : ℕ) [NeZero f] :
    Subsingleton (Pic (intAddMulOrder K f)) ↔ IsPrincipalIdealRing (𝓞 K) ∧
      (f = 1 ∨ (f = 2 ∧ NumberField.discr K % 8 = 1) ∨
        (NumberField.discr K = -3 ∧ (f = 2 ∨ f = 3)) ∨ (NumberField.discr K = -4 ∧ f = 2)) := by
  have h := card_pic_intAddMulOrder_eq_one_iff hK f
  rw [Nat.card_eq_one_iff_unique,
    and_iff_left (inferInstance : Nonempty (Pic (intAddMulOrder K f))),
    Nat.card_eq_fintype_card, ← NumberField.classNumber, NumberField.classNumber_eq_one_iff] at h
  exact h

/-- **Triviality of `Gal(H_{O_f} / K)` for imaginary quadratic orders**, read off
`ringClassArtinEquiv` and `card_pic_intAddMulOrder_eq_one_iff`. -/
theorem subsingleton_gal_ringClassField_intAddMulOrder_iff (hK : Module.finrank ℚ K = 2) (f : ℕ)
    [NeZero f] :
    Subsingleton Gal(ringClassField (intAddMulOrder K f)/K) ↔ IsPrincipalIdealRing (𝓞 K) ∧
      (f = 1 ∨ (f = 2 ∧ NumberField.discr K % 8 = 1) ∨
        (NumberField.discr K = -3 ∧ (f = 2 ∨ f = 3)) ∨ (NumberField.discr K = -4 ∧ f = 2)) :=
  (subsingleton_gal_ringClassField_iff (intAddMulOrder K f)).trans
    (subsingleton_pic_intAddMulOrder_iff hK f)

/-- **Classification of imaginary quadratic orders whose ring class field equals `K`.** -/
theorem ringClassField_intAddMulOrder_eq_bot_iff (hK : Module.finrank ℚ K = 2) (f : ℕ)
    [NeZero f] :
    ringClassField (intAddMulOrder K f) = ⊥ ↔ IsPrincipalIdealRing (𝓞 K) ∧
      (f = 1 ∨ (f = 2 ∧ NumberField.discr K % 8 = 1) ∨
        (NumberField.discr K = -3 ∧ (f = 2 ∨ f = 3)) ∨ (NumberField.discr K = -4 ∧ f = 2)) :=
  (ringClassField_eq_bot_iff (intAddMulOrder K f)).trans
    (subsingleton_pic_intAddMulOrder_iff hK f)

end ImaginaryQuadratic

/-! ### The nonmaximal order `ℤ + 2ℤ[i]` in `ℚ(i)` -/

section GaussianOrderTwo

variable (K : Type) [Field K] [NumberField K] [IsCyclotomicExtension {4} ℚ K]

private theorem discr_four : NumberField.discr K = -4 := by
  have hζ := IsCyclotomicExtension.zeta_spec 4 ℚ K
  exact GaussianRationals.discr_eq_neg_four hζ.minpoly_toInteger_eq_X_sq_add_one
    (IsCyclotomicExtension.adjoin_primitive_root_eq_top hζ)

private theorem isTotallyComplex_four : IsTotallyComplex K :=
  GaussianRationals.isTotallyComplex
    (IsCyclotomicExtension.zeta_spec 4 ℚ K).minpoly_toInteger_eq_X_sq_add_one

/-- **The order `ℤ + 2ℤ[i]` in `ℚ(i)` has discriminant `-16`.** -/
@[simp]
theorem discr_intAddMulOrder_two_four : (intAddMulOrder K 2).discr = -16 := by
  rw [discr_intAddMulOrder_of_finrank_eq_two
      (finrank_eq_two_of_isCyclotomicExtension_four (K := K)),
    discr_four K]
  norm_num

/-- The conductor of `ℤ + 2ℤ[i]` in `ℚ(i)` is `2 𝓞 K`. -/
theorem conductor_intAddMulOrder_two_four :
    (intAddMulOrder K 2).conductor = Ideal.span {(2 : 𝓞 K)} :=
  conductor_intAddMulOrder (finrank_eq_two_of_isCyclotomicExtension_four (K := K)) 2

/-- **The unit index `[(𝓞 K)ˣ : (ℤ + 2ℤ[i])ˣ]` in `ℚ(i)` is `2`**: `(𝓞 K)ˣ = {±1, ±i}` while only
`±1` lie in `ℤ + 2ℤ[i]`. -/
@[simp]
theorem index_range_unitsMap_intAddMulOrder_two_four :
    (Units.map ((intAddMulOrder K 2).toRingOfIntegers.val :
      (intAddMulOrder K 2).toRingOfIntegers →* 𝓞 K)).range.index = 2 := by
  have := isTotallyComplex_four K
  rw [index_range_unitsMap_intAddMulOrder (finrank_eq_two_of_isCyclotomicExtension_four (K := K)),
    discr_four K]
  decide

/-- **The residue ring `𝓞 K ⧸ 2 𝓞 K` of `ℚ(i)` has `2` units**: `2` ramifies in `ℚ(i)`
(`χ_{-4}(2) = 0`), so `#(𝓞 K ⧸ 2 𝓞 K)ˣ = (2 - 1)(2 - 0) = 2`. -/
@[simp]
theorem card_units_quotient_span_two_four :
    Nat.card (𝓞 K ⧸ Ideal.span {(2 : 𝓞 K)})ˣ = 2 := by
  have hK := finrank_eq_two_of_isCyclotomicExtension_four (K := K)
  have : Fact (Nat.Prime 2) := ⟨Nat.prime_two⟩
  have h := TauCeti.NumberField.card_units_quotient_span_natCast_of_prime hK 2
  have hχ : ∀ (D : ℤ) (hD : D.IsFundamentalDiscr), D = -4 →
      Multiquadratic.fundamentalDiscriminantChar D hD (2 : ℕ) = 0 := by
    rintro _ hD rfl
    rw [← Int.cast_natCast (R := ZMod _), Multiquadratic.fundamentalDiscriminantChar_neg_four]
    decide
  rw [hχ _ _ (discr_four K)] at h
  norm_num at h
  exact_mod_cast h

/-- The residue ring `(ℤ + 2ℤ[i]) ⧸ 2ℤ[i] ≃ ℤ/2ℤ` has `φ(2) = 1` unit. -/
@[simp]
theorem card_units_quotient_conductor_intAddMulOrder_two_four :
    Nat.card ((intAddMulOrder K 2).toRingOfIntegers ⧸ (intAddMulOrder K 2).conductor.comap
      ((intAddMulOrder K 2).toRingOfIntegers.val :
        (intAddMulOrder K 2).toRingOfIntegers →+* 𝓞 K))ˣ = 1 :=
  card_units_quotient_conductor_intAddMulOrder
    (finrank_eq_two_of_isCyclotomicExtension_four (K := K)) 2

/-- **`Pic (ℤ + 2ℤ[i])` has order `1`**: in the class number formula for orders, the residue-unit
count `#(𝓞 K ⧸ 2 𝓞 K)ˣ = 2` is cancelled by `#(ℤ/2ℤ)ˣ · [(𝓞 K)ˣ : Oˣ] = 1 · 2 = 2`. -/
@[simp]
theorem natCard_pic_intAddMulOrder_two_four :
    Nat.card (Pic (intAddMulOrder K 2)) = 1 := by
  have := isTotallyComplex_four K
  have := isPrincipalIdealRing_ringOfIntegers_four K
  exact Nat.card_eq_one_iff_unique.2 ⟨(subsingleton_pic_intAddMulOrder_iff
      (finrank_eq_two_of_isCyclotomicExtension_four (K := K)) 2).2
    ⟨inferInstance, Or.inr (Or.inr (Or.inr ⟨discr_four K, rfl⟩))⟩, inferInstance⟩

/-- `Pic (ℤ + 2ℤ[i])` is a subsingleton. -/
theorem subsingleton_pic_intAddMulOrder_two_four :
    Subsingleton (Pic (intAddMulOrder K 2)) :=
  (Nat.card_eq_one_iff_unique.1 (natCard_pic_intAddMulOrder_two_four K)).1

/-- **Through `ringClassArtinEquiv`, `Gal(ringClassField (ℤ + 2ℤ[i]) / ℚ(i))` is trivial.** -/
theorem subsingleton_gal_ringClassField_intAddMulOrder_two_four :
    Subsingleton Gal(ringClassField (intAddMulOrder K 2)/K) :=
  have := subsingleton_pic_intAddMulOrder_two_four K
  subsingleton_gal_ringClassField (intAddMulOrder K 2)

/-- **The ring class field of the nonmaximal order `ℤ + 2ℤ[i]` in `ℚ(i)` is `⊥` (`ℚ(i)`).** -/
@[simp]
theorem ringClassField_intAddMulOrder_two_four :
    ringClassField (intAddMulOrder K 2) = ⊥ :=
  have := subsingleton_pic_intAddMulOrder_two_four K
  ringClassField_eq_bot (intAddMulOrder K 2)

/-- **The ring class field of `ℤ + 2ℤ[i]` has degree `1` over `ℚ(i)`.** -/
@[simp]
theorem finrank_ringClassField_intAddMulOrder_two_four :
    Module.finrank K (ringClassField (intAddMulOrder K 2)) = 1 := by
  rw [finrank_ringClassField, natCard_pic_intAddMulOrder_two_four]

/-- **The Hilbert class field of `ℚ(i)` is `⊥`.** -/
@[simp]
theorem hilbertClassField_four : hilbertClassField K = ⊥ :=
  have := isPrincipalIdealRing_ringOfIntegers_four K
  hilbertClassField_eq_bot K

/-- **Every invertible proper fractional ideal of `ℤ + 2ℤ[i]` in `ℚ(i)` is principal**, since its
Artin symbol in the trivial Galois group `Gal(ringClassField (ℤ + 2ℤ[i]) / ℚ(i))` is `1`. -/
theorem isPrincipal_of_invertibleProperFractionalIdeals_intAddMulOrder_two_four
    (I : (intAddMulOrder K 2).invertibleProperFractionalIdeals) :
    (I : Submodule (intAddMulOrder K 2).toSubalgebra K).IsPrincipal := by
  have := subsingleton_gal_ringClassField_intAddMulOrder_two_four K
  exact (ringClassArtinMap_eq_one_iff (intAddMulOrder K 2) I).1 (Subsingleton.elim _ _)

/-- **Every maximal ideal of `ℤ[i]` prime to `2 ℤ[i]` has a generator in `ℤ + 2ℤ[i]`.** -/
theorem exists_mem_intAddMulOrder_two_span_eq_of_four
    (J : integralIdealsPrimeTo (intAddMulOrder K 2).conductorModulus)
    [(J : Ideal (𝓞 K)).IsMaximal] :
    ∃ β ∈ (intAddMulOrder K 2).toRingOfIntegers, (J : Ideal (𝓞 K)) = Ideal.span {β} := by
  have := subsingleton_pic_intAddMulOrder_two_four K
  exact exists_mem_toRingOfIntegers_span_eq_of_subsingleton_pic (intAddMulOrder K 2) J

/-- **Contrast for larger conductors in `ℚ(i)`**: for every `f > 2`, the ring class field of
`ℤ + f ℤ[i]` is a proper extension of `ℚ(i)` (`ringClassField (intAddMulOrder K f) ≠ ⊥`). -/
theorem ringClassField_intAddMulOrder_ne_bot_of_two_lt_of_four {f : ℕ} [NeZero f] (hf : 2 < f) :
    ringClassField (intAddMulOrder K f) ≠ ⊥ := by
  have := isTotallyComplex_four K
  rw [Ne, ringClassField_intAddMulOrder_eq_bot_iff
    (finrank_eq_two_of_isCyclotomicExtension_four (K := K)) f, discr_four K]
  rintro ⟨_, h⟩
  omega

end GaussianOrderTwo

/-! ### The maximal order of the cubic field `ℚ(ζ₇ + ζ₇⁻¹)` -/

section MaximalRealSeven

variable (L : Type) [Field L] [NumberField L] [IsCyclotomicExtension {7} ℚ L]

/-- The maximal order of `ℚ(ζ₇)⁺ = ℚ(ζ₇ + ζ₇⁻¹)` has discriminant `49`. -/
theorem discr_maximalNumberFieldOrder_maximalRealSubfield_seven :
    (maximalNumberFieldOrder (maximalRealSubfield L)).discr = 49 := by
  rw [discr_maximal, discr_maximalRealSubfield_seven L]

/-- **The Picard group of the maximal order of `ℚ(ζ₇ + ζ₇⁻¹)` has order `1`.** -/
theorem natCard_pic_maximalNumberFieldOrder_maximalRealSubfield_seven :
    Nat.card (Pic (maximalNumberFieldOrder (maximalRealSubfield L))) = 1 := by
  rw [natCard_pic_maximalNumberFieldOrder, classNumber_maximalRealSubfield_seven L]

/-- `Pic` of the maximal order of `ℚ(ζ₇ + ζ₇⁻¹)` is a subsingleton. -/
theorem subsingleton_pic_maximalNumberFieldOrder_maximalRealSubfield_seven :
    Subsingleton (Pic (maximalNumberFieldOrder (maximalRealSubfield L))) :=
  have := isPrincipalIdealRing_maximalRealSubfield_seven L
  subsingleton_pic_maximalNumberFieldOrder (maximalRealSubfield L)

/-- **Through `ringClassArtinEquiv`, `Gal(ringClassField (𝓞 L⁺) / L⁺)` is trivial** for the cubic
field `L⁺ = ℚ(ζ₇ + ζ₇⁻¹)`. -/
theorem subsingleton_gal_ringClassField_maximalRealSubfield_seven :
    Subsingleton Gal(ringClassField (maximalNumberFieldOrder (maximalRealSubfield L))/
      maximalRealSubfield L) :=
  have := subsingleton_pic_maximalNumberFieldOrder_maximalRealSubfield_seven L
  subsingleton_gal_ringClassField (maximalNumberFieldOrder (maximalRealSubfield L))

/-- **The ring class field of the maximal order of `ℚ(ζ₇ + ζ₇⁻¹)` is `⊥` (`ℚ(ζ₇ + ζ₇⁻¹)`).** -/
theorem ringClassField_maximalNumberFieldOrder_maximalRealSubfield_seven :
    ringClassField (maximalNumberFieldOrder (maximalRealSubfield L)) = ⊥ :=
  have := subsingleton_pic_maximalNumberFieldOrder_maximalRealSubfield_seven L
  ringClassField_eq_bot (maximalNumberFieldOrder (maximalRealSubfield L))

/-- **The Hilbert class field of `ℚ(ζ₇ + ζ₇⁻¹)` is `⊥`.** -/
@[simp]
theorem hilbertClassField_maximalRealSubfield_seven :
    hilbertClassField (maximalRealSubfield L) = ⊥ :=
  have := isPrincipalIdealRing_maximalRealSubfield_seven L
  hilbertClassField_eq_bot (maximalRealSubfield L)

/-- **The ring class field of the maximal order of `ℚ(ζ₇ + ζ₇⁻¹)` has degree `1` over
`ℚ(ζ₇ + ζ₇⁻¹)`.** -/
theorem finrank_ringClassField_maximalNumberFieldOrder_maximalRealSubfield_seven :
    Module.finrank (maximalRealSubfield L)
      (ringClassField (maximalNumberFieldOrder (maximalRealSubfield L))) = 1 := by
  rw [finrank_ringClassField, natCard_pic_maximalNumberFieldOrder_maximalRealSubfield_seven L]

end MaximalRealSeven

end TauCeti.ClassFieldTheory
